  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "YQfub2q7Mj7QN1WrV9WK5u+DNHg=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:42.843Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Flowable reference reads: *\"Flowable creates a technical audit trail (history) by default. When it is required to have a business audit trail, the audit task is the easiest way to do this.\"*\n\nThat sentence draws exactly the distinction an external decision-record layer is built on \u2014 execution history is not a record of decisions \u2014 and it appears in the vendor's own documentation rather than in a competitor's analysis.\n\nTwo implications follow. The distinction is legible to buyers in this category, so it does not need teaching, which lowers the cost of every conversation about it. And a vendor articulate enough to name the gap is likely to close it, which is what happened. Finding your thesis stated in a vendor's docs is simultaneously validation and a warning.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T08:45:42.843964Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:42.843968Z"
    }
  },
